<title>JAPAN: Japan Sept raw sugar imports down 19.2 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Sept raw sugar imports down 19.2 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's raw sugar imports in September totalled 101,952 tonnes, down 19.2 percent from a year earlier, Finance Ministry data released on Tuesday showed.</p>
<p>The breakdown was as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			  Sept 96	Aug 96	     Sept 95</p>
<p> Total		  101,952	185,087	    126,176</p>
<p> Main suppliers:</p>
<p> Thailand		32,395	 56,229	     34,611</p>
<p> Cuba			 nil	 18,499		   80</p>
<p> South Africa	   8,000	 37,496		  nil</p>
<p> Australia	     41,275	 70,865	     81,865</p>
<p> Fiji		    20,282	  1,996		9,620</p>
<p>Cumulative imports in the first nine months of this year totalled 1,147,742 tonnes against 1,210,642 tonnes during the same period last year.</p>
</text>
